- op: discuss  # fe89
  at: '2026-09-14T23:57:09Z'  # fe89
  by: agent  # fe89
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fe89
  clock: 7  # fe89
  nonce: fe89  # fe89
  message: "CLOSED ON BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE THROUGH THE PRODUCTION PATH, not on the unit\npredicate. Two Go functions in one fixture, built by build_repo_ddg, control\nprinted first:\n\n    CONTROL 'covered' walkable & NOT forfeited : True   ADMISSIBLE\n    'leak'            walkable & FORFEITED     : True   <- the filed shape\n\nBoth are WALKABLE -- both produce DDG edges, so both reach the gate. That\nmatters: the first fixture attempt put cwd's ONLY use in the range clause,\nwhich left the function with no edges at all, so it was never adjudicable and\nnever reached the gate. A forfeit measured on that shape would have proved\nnothing. The shipped fixture gives cwd a recorded use as well, so the function\nIS walkable and the range clause is a SECOND, unrecorded use -- which is the\nshape the item was filed for.\n\nA/B ON THE SAME FUNCTIONS, one variable changed:\n    leak     calls-only(OLD)=[]   widened(NEW)=[16]\n    covered  calls-only(OLD)=[]   widened(NEW)=[]\nOne row moves, the control does not. The old predicate returned an EMPTY set\nfor leak -- no forfeit, walk free to refute -- which is the defect.\n\nSHIPPED: uncovered_call_lines becomes uncovered_semantic_lines and asks for the\nunion of uncovered calls and uncovered SEMANTIC LEAVES (named, childless, not\npunctuation or comment), reusing the non-semantic skip list the CFG builder\nalready applies -- now extracted so the question has one spelling. The walk is\niterative; it recursed one frame per AST level, and here a RecursionError would\nhave been swallowed by the caller and read as \"no DDG edges\".\n\nDESIGN DECIDED ON THE RECORD, not on taste: a declared per-language list of\nbinding node types was rejected because that list is coextensive with \"what the\nextractor does not model\", which the walk's own docstring says is unknowable\nfrom inside it -- and this project has already run that experiment, with\natomic_statement missing from rust.yaml and typescript.yaml while both emitted\nzero DDG edges for months at 100% coverage.\n\nDISCLOSURE SHIPPED WITH IT, because a 18.8-51.6% forfeit rate that nothing\npublishes is the silent limitation ADR-0052 forbids: coverage_granularity moves\nlanguage -> function (its own R16 trigger had fired 19 days earlier and nobody\nnoticed, because the test guards the CONSTANT and nothing watched for the\nCONDITION), and dataflow_coverage now carries functions_walkable /\nfunctions_forfeited on both the JSON and text surfaces."  # fe89
